# WebOnOne v2 project

Agent skill: [.cursor/skills/webonone-agent/SKILL.md](../skills/webonone-agent/SKILL.md)

## Scope

`webonone-v2/frontend`, `webonone-v2/backend`, `webonone-v2/backend/migrations`.

Specs: [04-webonone-v2-project.md](../../spec/1.0.0/04-webonone-v2-project.md), [07-identity-webonone-integration.md](../../spec/1.0.0/07-identity-webonone-integration.md), [1.6.0 company feature](../../spec/1.6.0/README.md)

## Ports and env

| Layer | Port | Env file |
|-------|------|----------|
| Frontend | 3000 | `webonone-v2/frontend/.env` |
| Backend | 4000 | `webonone-v2/backend/.env` |

`JWT_SECRET` must match Identity backend. Super-admin seed: `SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL`, `SUPER_ADMIN_DISPLAY_NAME` (Identity account must use same email).

## Database

MySQL schema **`webonone_v2`** — themes, user preferences, site media refs, and **company tables** (`companies`, `company_memberships`, `super_admins`). Migrations run via `npm run migrate -w @webonone/webonone-backend`. Seed super admin via `npm run seed -w @webonone/webonone-backend`.

## Ownership

- `/login` redirects to Identity — **no local login forms**.
- `/callback` exchanges auth code for JWT via Identity API.
- JWT **verification** locally; no per-request Identity HTTP on hot paths.
- Basic Settings (`/settings/basic`) — company registration wizard and company section (spec 1.6.0).
- Company API is **native** to WebOnOne BE (`/api/v1/company/*`) — not a separate microservice.

Key paths: `features/settings/basic/`, `backend/src/routes/company.routes.ts`, `backend/src/services/company.service.ts`, `backend/src/middleware/auth.ts`, `backend/src/middleware/requireSuperAdmin.ts`.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root
```

Login flow requires Identity running (`npm run dev:identity`).

